From: macos-local research
Subject: [PATCH] 64B cache-line-aligned 2-way CPUJumpCache and inline L1 hit fastpath

Convert CPUJumpCache into 8,192 64-byte 2-way set-associative sets (16,384
entries total) with 1-bit LRU replacement and cached mmu_idx, eliminating
direct-mapped QHT fallback contention and indirect mmu_index virtual calls on
L1 hits. Split refills/misses into QEMU_NOINLINE tb_lookup_slow() so the
register-only L1 hit path inlines into helper_lookup_tb_ptr without stack
canaries or nested stack frames.

